# Registry caps (design/data/skills.toml): berserker is Rare (cap 3), great_sage is Legendary (cap 3,
# granted only on purpose). Expect: berserker granted to A, B, C and refused for D; great_sage granted to
# A, B, C and refused for D; `ttl registry` lists both at 3/3. Holders are keyed by UUID: `expect keyed` fails
# ("ttl: ...") when a record still names the player, and `legacy` + `migrate` rewrites A's records the old
# way (player name) and migrates them back. Every grant lands in `ttl registry history`.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRegA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRegB
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRegC
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRegD
@sleep 2
ttl grant TtlBotRegA berserker
ttl grant TtlBotRegB berserker
ttl grant TtlBotRegC berserker
ttl grant TtlBotRegD berserker
ttl grant TtlBotRegA great_sage
ttl grant TtlBotRegB great_sage
ttl grant TtlBotRegC great_sage
ttl grant TtlBotRegD great_sage
ttl registry
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotRegA berserker true
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotRegD berserker false
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotRegD great_sage false
ttl registry expect has TtlBotRegD berserker false
ttl registry expect keyed TtlBotRegA
ttl registry expect last TtlBotRegC great_sage grant
ttl registry history berserker
# Records written before UUID keys (the player's name) are migrated at login/start, or by /ttl registry migrate.
ttl registry legacy TtlBotRegA
ttl registry migrate
ttl registry expect keyed TtlBotRegA
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotRegA berserker true
# A reset gives the slots back (and logs a revoke).
ttl reset TtlBotRegA
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotRegA berserker false
ttl registry expect last TtlBotRegA revoke great_sage
ttl reset TtlBotRegB
ttl reset TtlBotRegC
ttl reset TtlBotRegD
ttl registry history
ttlbot remove TtlBotRegA
ttlbot remove TtlBotRegB
ttlbot remove TtlBotRegC
ttlbot remove TtlBotRegD
